<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Talikota</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1565">1565</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Rakkasa-Tangadi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Talikota was fought in January 1565 in the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a> and an alliance of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-sultanates">Deccan sultanates</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bijapur">Bijapur</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmadnagar">Ahmadnagar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golconda-fort">Golconda</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bidar">Bidar</a>. Vijayanagara's regent, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aliya-rama-raya">Aliya Rama Raya</a>, was captured and killed, his army collapsed, and the victors sacked the capital, Vijayanagara. The defeat ended the empire's dominance of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p></div>
